<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 10 May, from 28 BCE to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/china" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/china.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">28 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,053 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Han astronomers record China's first precisely dated sunspot</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the reign of Emperor Cheng of Han, Chinese astronomers made the first precisely dated sunspot observation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. The astronomer Gan De of the State of Qi had recognised sunspots as solar phenomena in the 4th century BCE.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1503">1503 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">523 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sights the Cayman Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his fourth voyage, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> sighted two small islands teeming with turtles, which he named Las Tortugas. They later became known as the Cayman Islands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1773">1773 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">253 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parliament passes the Tea Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Act let the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> ship <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> directly to America, undercutting smugglers while keeping the Townshend duty. Colonists saw it as a ploy to make them accept taxation, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston-tea-party">Boston Tea Party</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Second Continental Congress meets in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from the colonies gathered weeks after Lexington and Concord. The Congress created the Continental Army, appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> to command it and declared independence in 1776.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson dies of pneumonia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eight days after being wounded by his own men at Chancellorsville, General Thomas 'Stonewall' Jackson died. Lee said he had lost his right arm.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union cavalry capture Jefferson Davis in Georgia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The fleeing Confederate president was seized near Irwinville, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. He was held for two years at Fort Monroe but never brought to trial.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1869">1869 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Golden spike completes the first transcontinental railroad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Central Pacific and Union Pacific lines met at Promontory Summit, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a>. Coast-to-coast travel fell from months to about a week, at great cost to Native American lands.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Churchill becomes Prime Minister as Germany attacks in the West</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As German forces invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and Luxembourg, Neville Chamberlain resigned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> formed a coalition government to lead <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 10 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/meng-zhixiang"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Meng Zhixiang</span><span class="tp">874–934</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-nicolas-davout"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-nicolas-davout.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis-Nicolas Davout</span><span class="tp">1770–1823</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gustav-stresemann"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gustav-stresemann.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gustav Stresemann</span><span class="tp">1878–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/heydar-aliyev"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/heydar-aliyev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Heydar Aliyev</span><span class="tp">1923–2003</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hugo-banzer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hugo-banzer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hugo Banzer</span><span class="tp">1926–2002</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 10 May <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-xv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis XV</span><span class="tp">1710–1774</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andres-bonifacio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andres-bonifacio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andrés Bonifacio</span><span class="tp">1863–1897</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/konrad-henlein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/konrad-henlein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Konrad Henlein</span><span class="tp">1898–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leonid-kravchuk"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leonid-kravchuk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leonid Kravchuk</span><span class="tp">1934–2022</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
